.TH DMIDIPLAYER 1 "2026-10-02" "Gosh MIDI Player 2.0.0-alpha.1"
.SH NAME
dmidiplayer \- MIDI and karaoke player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dmidiplayer
[OPTIONS] [MIDI_FILES_OR_PLAYLISTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rust and Dioxus Desktop MIDI player for MID, MIDI, KAR, RMI and WRK files.
FluidSynth and native external MIDI outputs are available.
This version is a prerelease; see the repository validation record.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-portable
Use settings in the working directory.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file PATH
Use an explicit portable settings file.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-driver BACKEND
Select ALSA (Linux), MIDI (Windows/macOS), FluidSynth or Dummy.
Must be used with --connection. Dummy is intentionally silent.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-connection PORT
Select the output destination together with --driver.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Decode actual inputs without a GUI; invalid/missing inputs fail.
.TP
.B \-\-dump-info
Decode and print JSON metadata without a GUI.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat remaining arguments as paths.
.SH DATA
Linux configuration normally resides in ~/.config/dmidiplayer/dmidiplayer.conf.
Windows/macOS use native application-data locations.
Legacy key-file data and ~/.dmidiplayer song mixes remain readable.
Playlist files contain one path per line, with relative paths resolved against
that playlist's directory. Writes use atomic replacement.
